meta {
  name: 06 - Get Company Full Detail (Blocks)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/blocks?id={{company_item_id}}&maxDepth=-1&fetchMetadata=true
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  id: {{company_item_id}}
  maxDepth: -1
  fetchMetadata: true
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{craft_token}}
}

docs {
  Discovery step 5 (corrected model): collection items here are one per
  COMPANY, not one per job offer - offers live as nested blocks under each
  company (job links + "- [ ] Commencé la candidature ?" checklist items),
  and only some companies have them.

  This fetches the full block tree (maxDepth=-1, no truncation) for one
  company so we can see the real JSON `type`/`textStyle` of those checklist
  items and their block ids - that's what decides whether "mark applied"
  means flipping a dedicated `checked` field via PUT /blocks, or editing
  markdown text (`- [ ]` -> `- [x]`).

  Defaults to Linkedin's item id (small preview - "...and 1 more block"),
  a good first sample since its preview already showed one offer + one
  checklist item. Swap `company_item_id` to try others for a second data point.

  Read-only, safe to run freely.
}
